WEBVTT

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.980
College is not only a place to gain knowledge but also a place to learn how to get along with others.
大学不仅是获取知识的地方，也是学习如何与他人相处的地方。

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:15.000
For college students, developing social skills is a necessity rather than a choice.
对大学生来说，培养社交能力是必需的，而不是一种可有可无的选择。

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:19.320
First, good social skills make college life smoother and happier.
首先，良好的社交能力让大学生活更顺利、更快乐。

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:27.760
Students who communicate well find it easier to make friends, resolve conflicts with roommates and work effectively in group projects.
善于沟通的学生会发现更容易交到朋友、化解与室友的矛盾，并在小组项目中高效合作。

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:31.670
Second, social skills are essential for future careers.
其次，社交能力对未来的职业至关重要。

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:38.840
Employers value graduates who can express their ideas clearly, cooperate with colleagues and deal with clients.
雇主看重那些能清楚表达自己想法、与同事合作并与客户打交道的毕业生。

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:46.120
No matter how much knowledge students have, they will find it hard to succeed without the ability to work with others.
无论学生拥有多少知识，如果没有与他人合作的能力，他们都会发现很难取得成功。

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:54.710
Moreover, social skills help students build a wide network of relationships, which can provide support and opportunities in the future.
此外，社交能力能帮助学生建立广泛的人际关系网，将来可以为他们提供支持和机会。

00:00:55.510 --> 00:01:00.860
For these reasons, college students should seize every chance to improve their social skills.
由于这些原因，大学生应该抓住每一个机会提高自己的社交能力。

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:05.980
They can join clubs, do volunteer work and speak up in class discussions.
他们可以参加社团、做志愿者工作，并在课堂讨论中大胆发言。

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:13.060
Step by step, they will become confident communicators ready for the challenges of work and life ahead.
一步一步地，他们将成为自信的沟通者，做好准备迎接未来工作和生活中的挑战。
